description.narrative:
Power of Voices FAIR capacity development for strengthened civil society to lobby and advocate for fair agricultural value chains in Mozambique specifically Zambezia region at the district (District of Mocuba, Gurue and Alto Molocue) and Central level (City of Maputo).

The Project will be implemented and lead by Oxfam in Mozambique and partners ( The Centre for Democracy and Development  - CDD and The Development Support Association - NANA) and SOMO, has four focus areas:

1) Support the developmentof and promote alternatives to current business practices, and partnerships among value-chain actors based on viable business proposals;
2) Support civil society to engage and collaborate with the government;
3) Empower small-scale farmers in agricultural value chains (sesame and onion); strengthen institutions to increase access to markets; improve the competitiveness of small-scale agriculture; increase small-scale producer incomes and wages;
4) Support the development of legal frameworks for effective taxation of the extractives industry, including research on tax treaties tax trainings; support the investment of revenues in the sustainable development of inclusive agricultural value chains.

The programme is also expected to directly benefit some40,000 smallholders who are emerging commercial farmers, through investments in value chain development that will improve the security of their input supply and markets for their produce. The programme will ensure that women benefit equally from its interventions by requiring a minimum percentage of women as beneficiaries. Partner organizations will be required to have expertise in working on gender issues and using participatory techniques, and community mobilization activities will use mechanisms thathelp ensure participation. Different demands and expectations of male and female beneficiaries will be considered as part of the beneficiary feedback mechanisms.
